{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784312507,"nonce":"aUrk4k7/9NmmDY8RIpOAro1xdx8=","title":"[dogfood] Helm executor Role missing secrets RBAC — clone-token Secret never created, checkout Pod stuck FailedMount","message":"On a hardened in-cluster deploy (deploy/helm/scarab), the executor Role (templates/rbac.yaml) granted verbs on pods, pods/log, pods/status, pods/exec — but NOT secrets. The k8s executor upserts per-Pod Secrets before a step runs: the clone token (ADR-0045 GIT_ASKPASS tmpfs), the per-attempt OIDC token (ADR-0015), and a build step registry dockerconfig (ADR-0018) — ensure_clone_secret/ensure_oidc_secret/ensure_registry_secret in crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs. secrets.create() 403'd, so the clone-token Secret was never created; the checkout Pod (mounts secret \u003cpod\u003e-token) sat in Pending/FailedMount forever.\n\nAggravated by a latent race: K8sExecutor::launch treats create-409 (Pod exists) as successful re-attach and returns Ok WITHOUT ensure_clone_secret (lib.rs:677), unlike fresh-create (:670) and get_opt re-attach (:652). The 409-loser reported success and the run moved to poll(), so the Secret was never recreated.\n\nFix (committed): add resources:[secrets] verbs:[get,create,update] to the executor Role. Follow-up: also call ensure_clone_secret on the 409 branch.","files":null}]}